  "reference": "Spiegelhalter DJ, Stat Med 2005;24:1185-1202, Appendix A.1.1 \u2014 funnel plot for cross-sectional proportions: points sorted by denominator, runs signals suppressed, and exact binomial 99.8% / 95% contours with Spiegelhalter's continuity interpolation (r - alpha)/n in place of 3-sigma. ucl[0] is the interpolated Binomial(45, 0.1494505) 0.999 quantile plus one, divided by 45. Clinic H (70/310 = 22.6%) still breaches the funnel UCL. The published over-dispersion estimate is reported but not applied: phi-hat = 0.617 < (K-1)/K, so tau-hat = 0. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
